{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc / 0.610 F1, modestly above the best RNA-only (config_002: 0.591). The image-only model is very weak (0.208), so the ~2.8-point multimodal gain is small and its source is uncertain. Uncertainty: We have only tested concat fusion in the multimodal setting; we do not yet know whether the image modality carries a signal that benefits from learned re-weighting or whether concat already captures the useful interaction. Question tested: config_019 is identical to config_018 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, isolating the effect of fusion strategy. Why best next: It is a minimal, clean A/B comparison against the current best, directly resolving whether the image contribution is meaningful enough to warrant adaptive weighting. If weighted fusion improves performance, it justifies further investment in stronger image encoders (ViT-L); if it does not, concat is sufficient and budget is better spent exploring RNA-side improvements or confirming the image ceiling. This single experiment reduces the most consequential uncertainty about the multimodal design at the lowest cost."
}

